## If no sink points at the bucket (Console)

1. Logging → Log Router → Create sink.
2. Name: `route-to-me2`. Next.
3. Sink destination: Cloud Logging bucket → `cn-staging-logs-me2`.
4. Inclusion filter: paste this, which is your `_Default` filter exactly:
```
NOT LOG_ID("cloudaudit.googleapis.com/activity") AND NOT LOG_ID("externalaudit.googleapis.com/activity") AND NOT LOG_ID("cloudaudit.googleapis.com/system_event") AND NOT LOG_ID("externalaudit.googleapis.com/system_event") AND NOT LOG_ID("cloudaudit.googleapis.com/access_transparency") AND NOT LOG_ID("externalaudit.googleapis.com/access_transparency")
```
5. Exclusion filter: name `exclude-key-debug`, with:
```
logName="projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/logs/backend_pm2_out" AND jsonPayload.message:"DDDDDD"
```
6. Create sink.

Add the same exclusion to the `_Default` sink so the key line isn't stored globally either: Log Router → `_Default` → Edit → add exclusion → Update.

The filter above leaves out Admin Activity audit logs, because `_Required` keeps those globally. A sink can also copy them into the new bucket as a regional copy, but that doesn't remove the global one and it adds ingestion cost. I'd leave them out unless compliance asks for it.

